Change control is the process that IT department uses to identify, document, and authorize changes made to an IT environment. 

----
Sanitization involves securely erasing data from hard drives to ensure it can't be recovered or accessed by unauthorized individuals. 

-----
- Confidential - Very sensitive, must be approved to view 
-  Public / Unclassified - No restrictions on viewing the data 
-  Private / Classified / Restricted – Restricted access, may require an NDA 
-  Critical - Data should always be available
- Sensitive - Intellectual property, PII, PHI

Trade secret is the correct classification for data that is crucial for maintaining a competitive advantage and is deliberately kept secret within a company.

Intellectual Property: legally registered works that may be publicly disclosed through patents or copyrights.

Regulated data pertains to information subject to specific legal or regulatory requirements

private data refers to personal or sensitive information about individuals

