An expansionary risk appetite involves accepting higher levels of risk to capitalize on growth opportunities, typical of startups that prioritize speed and innovation. 

Conservative risk appetite indicates a preference for lower risk and stability. 

Neutral risk appetite suggests a balanced approach to risk-taking. 

The term risk-averse generally refers to a conservative approach and doesn’t align with the startup’s risk-taking strategy in the scenario.


-----
Stateful packet inspection (SPI) is appropriate for protecting against IP spoofing and other complex network attacks. 

Unlike stateless packet filtering, which inspects each packet in isolation, SPI keeps track of ongoing connections, allowing it to distinguish between legitimate and malicious packets more effectively.

Circuit-level gateways and application-level gateways (ALGs) are also important, but they serve different purposes and do not offer the same level of protection against IP spoofing.
